# EXERCISE MODEL

Version 1.0

---

# Purpose

This document defines the universal model used by the Combat Athlete System (CAS) to describe, classify and reason about every exercise.

Within CAS, an exercise is not simply a movement.

It is a structured object containing biomechanical, physiological, neurological and practical information.

Every exercise in the knowledge base inherits this model.

---

# Philosophy

Exercises are tools.

They are never objectives.

CAS never selects an exercise because it is popular.

CAS selects an exercise because it solves a specific performance problem.

Every recommendation must therefore be explainable.

---

# Definition

An exercise is a structured intervention designed to produce one or more specific adaptations.

Each exercise possesses measurable characteristics that determine:

Its purpose.

Its benefits.

Its limitations.

Its risks.

Its transfer to combat performance.

---

# Exercise Classification

CAS classifies every exercise using multiple independent dimensions.

An exercise never belongs to only one category.

Instead, it possesses a complete performance profile.

---

