# Success Criteria

The Exercise Model succeeds when:

Every exercise can be described consistently.

Every exercise can be compared objectively.

Every recommendation is explainable.

Exercise selection remains individualized.

Scientific consistency is maintained.

---

# Final Principle

Exercises are not the goal.

Adaptation is the goal.

CAS selects the exercise that creates the greatest probability of producing the desired adaptation,

for the right athlete,

at the right time,

with the lowest acceptable risk.